Upstream bug: direct /model/info?litellm_model_id=... lookups bypass the model
filter used by the endpoint's listing form. Upstream applies only the
listing's team scope to them.

Answer a direct-ID read outside the caller's models as upstream answers one
outside their teams: not found, or an empty list with include_team_models.

Removal check: model-info scope check in tests/verify_jwt_auth.py

diff --git a/litellm/proxy/proxy_server.py b/litellm/proxy/proxy_server.py
--- a/litellm/proxy/proxy_server.py
+++ b/litellm/proxy/proxy_server.py
@@ -18617,6 +18617,16 @@ async def model_info_v1(
         if _byok_row_outside_caller_teams(
             deployment_info.model_info.model_dump(),
             await _get_caller_byok_team_scope(user_api_key_dict, prisma_client),
+        ) or not _filter_v1_model_info_deployments(
+            # Direct-ID reads must enforce the same model scope as listings.
+            all_models=[deployment_info.model_dump(exclude_none=True)],
+            allowed_model_names=await _get_v1_model_info_allowed_model_names_with_access_groups(
+                user_api_key_dict=user_api_key_dict,
+                llm_router=llm_router,
+                prisma_client=prisma_client,
+                user_api_key_cache=user_api_key_cache,
+                proxy_logging_obj=proxy_logging_obj,
+            ),
         ):
             if include_team_models:
                 return _model_info_json_response([])
